## Context

Reading-2 findings 19–20 (tracker 0578). Figure 5 (fig:reliability,
`fig_exp1_reliability.pdf`) lost the per-model-family colors — a
regression: `src/aedist/plot_exp1_reliability.py` paints every dot with
the single `COLOR_MATCHED` constant and does not import
`model_family_color` (unlike `plot_exp2_arms_comparison.py` and
`plot_exp2_coverage_certainty.py`, which use it). Separately, the
`deepseek-v4-flash` point label overlaps; it must be placed to the left
(the `JITTER_SIDE` dict at ~L106 has `deepseek-v4-pro: "left"` but no
entry for `deepseek-v4-flash`).

Pure figure-code work: no main.tex edit, parallelizable with the
main.tex chain (no Blocked-by).

## Relevant files

- `src/aedist/plot_exp1_reliability.py` — the plot script to fix
- `src/aedist/plot_exp2_arms_comparison.py` — reference implementation
  of `model_family_color` usage (per-agent `_AGENT_MODEL` dict)
- `experiments/render.mk:290–292` — Makefile rule producing
  `$(ANALYSIS_GEN)/fig_exp1_reliability.pdf`
- `report/inputs/generated/fig_exp1_reliability.pdf` — committed
  handoff artifact, regenerate and commit
- `tickets/0574-…` — deterministic-PDF metadata ticket touches the same
  `savefig` calls; coordinate (land either first, rebase the other)

## Actions

1. Color the scatter points by model family via `model_family_color`
   (same util the exp2 plots import); keep matched/unmatched or other
   semantic encodings the figure already carries.
2. Add `"deepseek-v4-flash": "left"` to the label-side dict.
3. Rebuild the figure via the render.mk target; commit script + PDF.

## Test

- Red first: a unit test (source-inspection style per coding rules) in
  `tests/` asserting `plot_exp1_reliability.py` references
  `model_family_color` and that the label-side mapping contains
  `deepseek-v4-flash`. Goes red on current code, green after the fix.

